  "result": "Excellent! All 112 tests pass. Here's what I implemented:\n\n**Date Utilities Module**\n\n1. **`src/dates.js`** \u2014 Three functions for consistent UTC date handling:\n   - `isValidDate(text)`: Validates YYYY-MM-DD format and verifies the date is real (catches invalid dates like 2024-02-30 and non-leap-year Feb 29)\n   - `addDays(date, n)`: Adds n days to a date string, returns new YYYY-MM-DD string, uses UTC arithmetic\n   - `daysBetween(a, b)`: Returns b - a in whole days using UTC arithmetic\n\n2. **`src/invoices.js`** \u2014 Updated `createInvoice()`:\n   - Replaced manual date validation with `isValidDate()` call\n   - Now delegates all date handling to the utility module\n\n3. **`test/dates.test.js`** \u2014 Comprehensive test suite with 17 tests:\n   - Format validation (accepts valid YYYY-MM-DD, rejects malformed strings)\n   - Date validation (catches invalid dates like Feb 30, month 13, day 0)\n   - Leap year handling (2024 is leap, 1900 isn't, 2000 is)\n   - `addDays()` with positive/negative values and boundary cases (month/year transitions)\n   - `daysBetween()` calculations in both directions\n   - Cross-consistency: `daysBetween(a, addDays(a, n))` always equals `n`\n\nAll 112 tests pass \u2713",
